TEXT 472 104 Left 2 ;You can alternatively plot the active power of transformer primary side by adding\nthe following expressions to the waveformviewer:\n \nfor P of phaseA: v(n006)*Ix(Transformer1:1U)   xaxis: 200ms-400ms + ctrlclick = AVG = 9.63 MW\n \nfor P of phaseB: v(n0010)*Ix(Transformer1:1V)  xaxis: 200ms-400ms + ctrlclick = AVG = 0.614 MW\n  \nfor P of phaseC: v(n0014)*Ix(Transformer1:1W)  xaxis: 200ms-400ms + ctrlclick = AVG = 20.147 MW\n \nHINT: For fast access to the sum of all three measurement values (All three phases) you can:\nSet xaxis to 200ms-400ms, ALT+Click to the transformer symbol. Now you get the powerlost of transformer1\nWaveform expression is: Sum of active power over primary AND secondary side of the transformer = powerlost = 252kW\nV(N006)*Ix(Transformer1:1U)+V(N010)*Ix(Transformer1:1V)+V(N014)*Ix(Transformer1:1W)+\nV(N007)*Ix(Transformer1:2U)+V(N011)*Ix(Transformer1:2V)+V(N015)*Ix(Transformer1:2W)+V(P001)*Ix(Transformer1:2N)\nNow you can delete the last four terms to get the sum of active power only for the primary side of the transformer. \nNow Ctrl+click at the expression to get the avg active power over all three phases = 30.4MW\nThis is much simpler as to compute the FFT values to get the active power!\nBut to get also the reactive power - FFT is needed
