TEXT 472 64 Left 2 ;NOTE: The active and reactive power of higher frequencies (100,150,200Hz)\nis zero because there is no driving voltage with higher frequencies present !!
TEXT 472 456 Left 2 ;NOTE: To get the active power of primary side of the transformer of all three phases for 1200ms-1400ms:\nAlt + click on the transformer: to get the powerlost\nV(N006)*Ix(Transformer1:1U)+V(N010)*Ix(Transformer1:1V)+V(N014)*Ix(Transformer1:1W)+\nV(N007)*Ix(Transformer1:2U)+V(N011)*Ix(Transformer1:2V)+V(N015)*Ix(Transformer1:2W)+V(P001)*Ix(Transformer1:2N)\nNow you can delete the last four terms to get the sum of active power only for the primary side of the transformer. \nNow Ctrl+click at the expression to get the avg active power over all three phases = 15.3MW
